# nelisp-thread-standalone-smoke: Doc 199 Tier 2 Shape B.  The smoke is
# loaded by target/nelisp itself (not self-host compiled), spawns three fixed
# registry worker-ID 1 clone(2) tasks, publishes three distinct result slots
# through a shared SeqCst done counter + join, and requires 14+14+14=42.
# The gate-mutations row suppresses the worker result store, proving this gate
# detects a worker that completes but publishes the wrong result.
nelisp-thread-standalone-smoke
# nelisp-thread-allocating-standalone-smoke: Doc 199 Tier 3a feasibility
# spike.  Registry worker ID 2 evaluates pre-built ordinary Lisp through
# nelisp_eval_call with a private mmap EvalCtx, fresh lexical frame stack, and
# private native clone stack.  The bounded section inhibits collection,
# disables the non-atomic sweep free-list so allocators use the CAS bump path,
# preflights 8 MiB in the current chunk, and rejects chunk growth at exit.
# Checkpoint 1 publishes length 5 from one allocating worker.  Checkpoint 2
# barriers three workers while their private frames hold live allocated lists,
# attempts garbage-collect on each, then requires 5+7+11=23 after join.
# The Makefile target repeats the smoke under `ulimit -v 4000000', the
# deterministic reproducer for the Stage 4c empty-chunk-unmap corruption.
# Mutation-proven by suppressing the unique parallel-active publication; the
# section-exit assertion then rejects the run deterministically.
nelisp-thread-allocating-standalone-smoke
# nelisp-thread-mirror-guard-standalone-smoke: the enforced Doc 199 Tier
# 3a/3b ceiling.  A registered ID-2 worker calls a global function and reads a
# global value successfully, then hit-path and miss-path setq attempts must
# raise the named catchable condition without changing/inserting mirror state.
# A fresh intern-table insertion is refused and remains absent as well.  The
# mutation row disables the reached registry-match branch and makes these
# assertions go red against a freshly rebuilt binary.
nelisp-thread-mirror-guard-standalone-smoke
# nelisp-thread-percpu-roots-smoke: Doc 199 Tier 3b's real park-barrier proof.
# Three registry-ID-2 allocating workers wait in join safepoints while private
# lexical frames hold live lists of lengths 5, 7, and 11.  Main-thread
# garbage-collect must request and observe parked=3, run one actual mark/sweep,
# resume the workers with missed-collects unchanged, and preserve 5+7+11=23;
# bounded-section exit must clear the registry.  The Makefile target runs once
# normally and five times under `ulimit -v 4000000'.  Its mutation corrupts the
# reached post-collection last-parked observation, so the mandatory count=3
# assertion necessarily turns red after the real collector path has run.
nelisp-thread-percpu-roots-smoke
#
